1
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:34,990
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,950
[Episode 17]

3
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,200
You know me?

4
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:56,070
I've heard of you.

5
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,310
You defected to our side in Hangzhou,

6
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,150
helping us take down

7
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:05,810
a Communist contact station.

8
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:10,110
After that, you also lured
and captured several Communists.

9
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:13,960
Your name has already come up
on Director Li's radar.

10
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:17,870
You flatter me, Section Chief Zhao.

11
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:23,470
I'm going to meet someone tomorrow.

12
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:24,670
The expert's coming?

13
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,950
He's a biological expert
returning from the Soviet Union.

14
00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:29,350
His hometown is Jiaxing,

15
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,750
and he's been home
visiting family for quite some time.

16
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,980
He'll be setting out for Shanghai
tomorrow.

17
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:36,640
I have to go meet him in person.

18
00:02:38,079 --> 00:02:39,680
Today when I was heading out,

19
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:40,680
I saw Captain Du

20
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:42,870
leaving with a big crowd of people.

21
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:46,520
Are you working on the same case as him?

22
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,329
Yes.

23
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:47,960
[Feiyang Teahouse]

24
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:02,000
You guys talk. I'll go have a smoke.

25
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,840
Section Chief Lu.

26
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,840
Captain Du.

27
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:19,769
Section Chief Lu, you certainly
have your sources.

28
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,950
You're too kind, Captain Du.

29
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:23,480
It was just a stroke of luck.

30
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,920
His name is Feng Shen.

31
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:29,410
He's already boarded a train
at Jiaxing Station.

32
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,240
He's extremely vigilant,

33
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:33,480
so we didn't follow too closely—

34
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,620
we were worried about being exposed

35
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,020
and missing our chance to apprehend Diana.

36
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:41,190
You've thought this through carefully,
Section Chief Lu.

37
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:42,190
If this goes well,

38
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,800
you'll deserve the biggest credit.

39
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:47,320
When the time comes, I'd appreciate it

40
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,240
if you could put in a good word for me

41
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,240
with Director Li, Captain Du.

42
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,240
Consider it done.

43
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,220
Spread these photos around.

44
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,400
Today's operation is to capture Diana.

45
00:05:35,150 --> 00:05:35,990
She's exposed.

46
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:37,440
Split up and find her. We must stop her.

47
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,150
Who is she?

48
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,590
Goodbye.

49
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,690
Section Chief Zhao.

50
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,800
I'll leave Section Chief Lu in your care.

51
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,430
Of course.

52
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:33,640
Section Chief Lu,
you haven't eaten yet, have you?

53
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,840
Let me get you a snack.

54
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:35,659
No need.

55
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:36,550
Please, let me.

56
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,940
It's an ambush.

57
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:16,150
Inspector Su?

58
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,720
What are you doing here?

59
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,400
Are you meeting someone?

60
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:30,160
I was the one who informed Inspector Su
that there was an operation today.

61
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,620
Behind Captain Du's back?

62
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,120
Captain Cang.

63
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,980
Do I need to report to you every time

64
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:47,840
I come to supervise an operation?

65
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:49,250
Sure you don't.

66
00:08:52,910 --> 00:08:54,150
But now that you're here, Inspector Su,

67
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:55,910
why don't you go see Captain Du?

68
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:26,800
Captain Cang.

69
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:29,360
What are you getting at?

70
00:09:30,410 --> 00:09:32,340
Today's operation is classified.

71
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,200
Everyone who shows up here

72
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:37,440
needs to have a valid reason for that.

73
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,120
Inspector Su, please come with me

74
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:43,710
and explain yourself to Captain Du.

75
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:16,650
Over there! Hurry!

76
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,460
What happened?

77
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,930
I was taking photos over there

78
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,240
when I suddenly heard gunshots,

79
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,080
so I ran over.

80
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:51,980
I saw someone running away.

81
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:52,750
Who?

82
00:10:53,330 --> 00:10:54,660
I didn't get a good look.

83
00:10:55,950 --> 00:10:58,550
He must have encountered that person
head-on.

84
00:10:58,630 --> 00:11:00,430
The bullet came straight at him.

85
00:11:05,150 --> 00:11:05,840
Follow me.

86
00:11:15,910 --> 00:11:16,970
Who did this to you?

87
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:23,600
Tell me, who did this?

88
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:31,080
Freeze!

89
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:18,800
Useless trash.

90
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,100
Did you shoot too?

91
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:48,750
After you,

92
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:49,800
Inspector Su.

93
00:12:58,630 --> 00:12:59,360
Go ahead and leave.

94
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:00,760
I'll handle the cleanup.

95
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,600
Can you handle it?

96
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:03,440
Just go.

97
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,320
I saw that person running away,

98
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:14,480
so I fired a shot.

99
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:20,790
Too bad I missed.

100
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:31,220
This is a shell casing
from a Japanese Nambu Type 14.

101
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,720
The caliber is smaller than your Browning.

102
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,060
Guns are meant for self-defense.

103
00:13:45,110 --> 00:13:47,800
If you ever find yourself in a situation
like this again, fire a few more shots.

104
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,410
Okay.

105
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,800
Take a picture of him,

106
00:13:54,930 --> 00:13:57,130
so we have something to show his family.

107
00:14:13,130 --> 00:14:13,930
Darn it.

108
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:17,800
Hurry up!

109
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,280
Let's go. Back to No. 76.

110
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:03,330
I can't believe they still got away.

111
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:06,280
Your information got through.

112
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,600
It's not your fault they got away.

113
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:21,450
But now my transfer to Shanghai
is off the table.

114
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,270
Section Chief Lu, you managed to find out

115
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:27,270
where Diana was supposed to make contact.

116
00:15:27,270 --> 00:15:29,200
You must have some special skills.

117
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,860
Director Li will certainly value

118
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:34,480
a talent like you.

119
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,150
Thank you, Section Chief Zhao,

120
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:39,210
for cheering me up.

121
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:46,710
I'd like to ask you something,
Section Chief Zhao.

122
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,080
There was a young man beside Captain Du

123
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,960
who carried a camera.

124
00:15:52,390 --> 00:15:53,030
Who is he?

125
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:56,550
That's the photographer Captain Du hired.

126
00:15:56,550 --> 00:15:58,550
He works in the Propaganda Section.

127
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,570
Then I wasn't mistaken.

128
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:23,890
He's from Hangzhou, right?

129
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:29,390
I think so.

130
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:32,110
His master was Li Musheng,

131
00:16:32,790 --> 00:16:33,790
a Communist

132
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,960
codenamed "Broken Bridge."

133
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,650
His name is Chen Kailai.

134
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,930
He's probably a Communist too.

135
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:42,710
He's clearly up to something

136
00:16:42,730 --> 00:16:44,890
by infiltrating Captain Du's inner circle.

137
00:16:44,890 --> 00:16:46,420
Let's wait here for a while.

138
00:16:46,590 --> 00:16:49,920
There's a distinguished guest
in Section Chief Zhao's car.

139
00:16:50,650 --> 00:16:51,820
Do you think my good luck

140
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,220
hasn't run out yet?

141
00:16:54,030 --> 00:16:55,160
Section Chief Zhao,

142
00:16:55,470 --> 00:16:57,720
isn't that a sign
that heaven's on my side?

143
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,390
Indeed.

144
00:16:59,270 --> 00:17:01,870
It really does seem like
heaven's on your side.

145
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,500
You're also a Communist!

146
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:24,140
Don't go.

147
00:17:26,230 --> 00:17:27,490
It's not appropriate.

148
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:31,740
Mr. Zhao.

149
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,120
You've kept yourself hidden for so long.

150
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,450
Why did you have to
let your guard down now?

151
00:19:01,790 --> 00:19:04,120
Why become a Communist in the first place?

152
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:16,030
Du Huangqiao.

153
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:20,400
Why did you join the Nationalist Army

154
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,270
back then?

155
00:19:24,410 --> 00:19:25,540
Have you forgotten?

156
00:19:29,230 --> 00:19:30,310
You should know

157
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:34,560
that in times like these,
people who have too good a memory

158
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:35,570
won't live long.

159
00:19:36,410 --> 00:19:38,470
What's the point of living that long?

160
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:43,280
I'm about to die.

161
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,540
Have Chen Kailai take a picture of me.

162
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,760
Who's "Leifeng Pagoda"?

163
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,200
Shanghai isn't an easy place to get by.

164
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,000
Be careful.

165
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,630
Your camera's American-made, right?

166
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:42,810
Sometimes what you see
isn't necessarily the truth.

167
00:20:46,590 --> 00:20:48,190
As long as we are still alive,

168
00:20:50,550 --> 00:20:52,400
there is hope to keep going.

169
00:20:53,590 --> 00:20:54,960
What is faith?

170
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,830
Probably something worth living for.

171
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:01,310
Will she be in danger?

172
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:07,510
Sincerity is the easiest thing to fake.

173
00:21:24,690 --> 00:21:25,380
Why go

174
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:28,510
this far?

175
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:31,550
If I'd known this day would come so soon,

176
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:34,210
I would've left you something
to remember me by.

177
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:38,010
I've got some pretty good liquor,

178
00:21:42,190 --> 00:21:44,790
but now I don't have time
to treat you to a drink.

179
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:49,790
I told you before—

180
00:21:50,390 --> 00:21:52,520
Shanghai isn't an easy place to get by.

181
00:21:58,070 --> 00:21:59,680
Tell me who Diana is,

182
00:22:00,790 --> 00:22:02,190
and I'll spare your life.

183
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:05,280
Du Huangqiao.

184
00:22:06,550 --> 00:22:07,610
You think you still

185
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:10,280
have the power to decide
whether I live or die?

186
00:22:13,510 --> 00:22:15,110
You're nothing but a lapdog.

187
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,160
Don't you fear death?

188
00:23:16,590 --> 00:23:17,390
Of course I do.

189
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:19,550
Who wouldn't?

190
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:23,360
Everyone dies eventually.

191
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:26,200
If I get to choose how I die,

192
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:29,440
wouldn't that be a blessing
in its own way?

193
00:23:31,510 --> 00:23:33,440
At least I'll die without regrets.

194
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:09,790
There's no gun on him.

195
00:24:13,750 --> 00:24:15,360
He was asking to be killed.

196
00:24:19,590 --> 00:24:20,720
If one day

197
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:23,220
I bid you farewell forever in battle,

198
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,090
please remember me as your friend.

199
00:24:27,420 --> 00:24:28,550
My name is Zhao Qian,

200
00:24:29,310 --> 00:24:31,660
nicknamed "Mr. Zhao."

201
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,480
Who would've thought

202
00:24:41,030 --> 00:24:42,590
there was a Communist spy

203
00:24:42,590 --> 00:24:44,250
hiding right under our noses?

204
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,100
Why do you think

205
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,110
he chose to make his move now,

206
00:24:48,110 --> 00:24:49,790
after hiding for so long?

207
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,400
Lu Xiaoguang was a Communist who defected.

208
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:55,070
Maybe

209
00:24:55,830 --> 00:24:57,830
he found out some secret about Zhao.

210
00:24:58,640 --> 00:24:59,800
Diana got away,

211
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:01,400
but we rooted out Zhao Qian.

212
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,800
So it wasn't a total loss.

213
00:25:03,750 --> 00:25:06,880
But Zhao Qian's defection
has to be reported to Nanjing.

214
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:08,750
How should we put it

215
00:25:08,750 --> 00:25:10,280
to make it sound inspiring—

216
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:12,110
you've got to have a plan in mind.

217
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:13,760
I understand.

218
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,160
Director.

219
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:19,640
Inspector Su might be involved in this.

220
00:25:21,510 --> 00:25:24,840
You mean the past relationship
between Su Men and Zhao Qian?

221
00:25:26,030 --> 00:25:27,630
There's more to it than that.

222
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:36,160
The Japanese Nambu Type 14—

223
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:41,480
Inspector Su's service pistol
uses the same caliber.

224
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:46,790
With all these coincidences piling up,

225
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,000
don't you think there's more to it?

226
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:50,960
You expect me

227
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,070
to tell Nanjing that

228
00:25:53,550 --> 00:25:55,080
Inspector Su is a suspect because of

229
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:57,810
some old romantic affairs
she had with Zhao Qian?

230
00:25:58,960 --> 00:25:59,640
Still,

231
00:26:00,550 --> 00:26:02,510
rooting out Communist infiltrators

232
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:03,480
is our duty.

233
00:26:04,550 --> 00:26:05,280
Understood.

234
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:07,660
I'll go find evidence right away.

235
00:26:30,510 --> 00:26:31,160
Hold on.

236
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:53,740
It's you, Captain Du.

237
00:27:57,110 --> 00:27:57,920
I'm guessing

238
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:01,120
the perfume you're wearing today,
Inspector Su,

239
00:28:01,120 --> 00:28:02,750
is a blend of lemon, orange,

240
00:28:03,270 --> 00:28:04,830
and lavender.

241
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:08,970
Your nose is sharp, Captain Du.

242
00:28:11,110 --> 00:28:15,040
It goes perfectly with the dance
you just performed, "Por Una Cabeza."

243
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:19,200
Captain Du, you didn't come here
this late at night

244
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,460
just to give me dancing lessons, did you?

245
00:28:24,350 --> 00:28:25,550
Sorry to disturb you.

246
00:28:26,350 --> 00:28:28,000
We're currently on the hunt

247
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:30,550
for a Communist who escaped
during an operation.

248
00:28:30,550 --> 00:28:31,720
We saw him

249
00:28:31,750 --> 00:28:33,950
jump over the wall into your courtyard.

250
00:28:36,310 --> 00:28:38,970
Are you suspecting me of
harboring a Communist?

251
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:41,030
Of course not.

252
00:28:41,870 --> 00:28:42,630
But

253
00:28:43,110 --> 00:28:45,170
to ensure your safety, Inspector Su,

254
00:28:45,510 --> 00:28:47,570
it'd be best if we searched the place.

255
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:56,140
With a reason like that from you,
Captain Du,

256
00:28:56,550 --> 00:28:57,550
I can't say no.

257
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:03,360
Go ahead and search then.

258
00:30:14,590 --> 00:30:16,720
If I'd known this day would come so soon,

259
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:19,380
I would've left you something
to remember me by.

260
00:30:19,460 --> 00:30:21,320
I've got some pretty good liquor.

261
00:30:56,910 --> 00:30:58,110
Nothing suspicious.

262
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:08,520
Inspector Su,

263
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,510
may I see your service pistol?

264
00:31:12,550 --> 00:31:13,270
Du,

265
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:15,160
don't push your luck.

266
00:31:20,350 --> 00:31:21,810
Since we've come this far,

267
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:23,780
we might as well
finish the proper procedure.

268
00:31:23,780 --> 00:31:25,740
What do you say, Inspector Su?

269
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:39,920
Captain Du,

270
00:31:41,110 --> 00:31:44,570
and what procedure requires you
to inspect my service pistol?

271
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,890
If I remember correctly,

272
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:49,890
Inspector Su, the service pistol
you have registered

273
00:31:49,890 --> 00:31:51,460
is a Japanese Nambu Type 14.

274
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:56,160
Your information isn't quite accurate,
Captain Du.

275
00:31:56,160 --> 00:31:57,160
That gun is broken

276
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:59,570
and has been out of service
for a long time.

277
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:02,200
Would you like me to hand it over
for inspection?

278
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:02,880
Please do.

279
00:32:04,750 --> 00:32:06,410
Go get it for Captain Du to see.

280
00:32:31,190 --> 00:32:33,560
This gun really is broken.

281
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,940
Anything else you'd like to ask,
Captain Du?

282
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:42,310
A Communist we're after

283
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:43,960
met with a Communist spy

284
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,220
codenamed Diana at Changding Alley

285
00:32:45,220 --> 00:32:47,980
at 3 p.m. this afternoon.

286
00:32:49,350 --> 00:32:52,410
May I ask what you were doing
at that time, Inspector Su?

287
00:32:59,180 --> 00:33:00,980
You suspect I'm a Communist spy?

288
00:33:04,350 --> 00:33:07,310
I'm just helping you
rule out any suspicion.

289
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,440
First you said

290
00:33:11,790 --> 00:33:14,250
someone saw a Communist
enter my courtyard,

291
00:33:14,550 --> 00:33:17,610
and now you're accusing me of
meeting with a Communist?

292
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:21,510
As far as I know,

293
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,550
Inspector Su, you left No. 76

294
00:33:23,550 --> 00:33:24,790
at 1:30 p.m. this afternoon

295
00:33:24,790 --> 00:33:26,310
and didn't return until 4 p.m.

296
00:33:26,310 --> 00:33:27,720
May I ask, where did you go

297
00:33:28,550 --> 00:33:29,550
during this time?

298
00:33:41,570 --> 00:33:43,830
My whereabouts are none of your concern.

299
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:47,300
In that case,

300
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:49,520
you're making my job rather difficult.

301
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:54,590
Du,

302
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:59,040
if you're looking for a fight,
you'd better pick the right place.

303
00:34:01,460 --> 00:34:02,260
Inspector Su,

304
00:34:03,070 --> 00:34:05,200
please forgive me if I've offended you.

305
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:07,440
I'm simply carrying out my orders.

306
00:34:07,460 --> 00:34:08,380
Orders?

307
00:34:08,739 --> 00:34:10,420
Orders to frame me?

308
00:34:11,159 --> 00:34:14,360
Captain Du, you need to think through
the consequences of your actions.

309
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,320
I, Du Huangqiao, am a lone wolf

310
00:34:16,570 --> 00:34:17,760
with nothing to lose.

311
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:19,889
I never worry about the consequences.

312
00:34:27,610 --> 00:34:28,940
I let you search my home,

313
00:34:30,550 --> 00:34:31,920
and I showed you my gun.

314
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:34,960
Du Huangqiao.

315
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,360
As for my whereabouts,

316
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,230
you're not qualified to ask.

317
00:34:38,230 --> 00:34:38,920
Let alone you,

318
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:41,050
even your boss doesn't have the right.

319
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:45,360
If you have evidence, produce it

320
00:34:46,210 --> 00:34:49,010
and have General Kagesa
come question me himself.

321
00:34:50,429 --> 00:34:51,510
Now get out.

322
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:07,230
Inspector Su, I'll report your words

323
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:09,110
truthfully to Director Li

324
00:35:09,110 --> 00:35:10,240
and General Kagesa.

325
00:35:35,070 --> 00:35:35,670
Hello?

326
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:37,320
Du Huangqiao found a shell casing

327
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:38,960
from your gun at the scene.

328
00:35:39,550 --> 00:35:41,950
You need to get rid of
the evidence quickly.

329
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:50,220
Go and disable the gun.

330
00:35:50,590 --> 00:35:51,360
Hurry!

331
00:36:16,410 --> 00:36:18,410
This is what Leifeng Pagoda asked me

332
00:36:19,150 --> 00:36:20,550
to pick up before he died.

333
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:30,630
I have a gift for you.

334
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:36,150
What's this?

335
00:36:36,710 --> 00:36:38,840
A copy I made of Yu Yingxiang's ledger.

336
00:36:39,320 --> 00:36:41,580
It contains Li Moqun's bribery records.

337
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,030
How did you get it?

338
00:36:47,510 --> 00:36:50,570
Well, I'm not the Logistics Section Chief
for nothing,

339
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:51,590
Diana.

340
00:36:57,670 --> 00:36:59,400
You've kept your cover so well.

341
00:37:00,340 --> 00:37:02,140
You might as well keep it for now.

342
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:11,280
This is the last gift he left us.

343
00:37:13,980 --> 00:37:15,380
Keep the negatives safe,

344
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:16,800
just in case.

345
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:23,060
He used to always carry this lighter.

346
00:37:23,630 --> 00:37:24,960
I picked it up

347
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:26,850
when they weren't looking.

348
00:38:31,070 --> 00:38:32,930
How's your dancing coming along?

349
00:38:33,070 --> 00:38:34,200
Still not very good.

350
00:38:42,730 --> 00:38:44,810
I used to dance with him a lot.

351
00:39:01,330 --> 00:39:02,560
He died because of me.

352
00:39:05,580 --> 00:39:07,440
That man's name was Lu Xiaoguang.

353
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:10,610
He was the traitor who betrayed my master.

354
00:39:14,150 --> 00:39:15,880
I'm just a lousy photographer.

355
00:39:17,190 --> 00:39:18,370
Besides taking pictures,

356
00:39:18,370 --> 00:39:19,570
I'm good for nothing.

357
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:23,760
I didn't even dare to fire a gun before.

358
00:39:27,230 --> 00:39:28,890
I wasn't worth his sacrifice.

359
00:39:31,030 --> 00:39:32,560
He didn't just do it for you.

360
00:39:39,270 --> 00:39:40,140
After tonight,

361
00:39:41,670 --> 00:39:43,330
we have to put our grief aside.

362
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:50,290
Du Huangqiao already suspects me.

363
00:39:51,990 --> 00:39:54,050
Li Moqun will definitely
seize this opportunity

364
00:39:54,050 --> 00:39:55,510
to make a big deal out of it.

365
00:39:57,630 --> 00:39:58,630
What do we do next?

366
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:14,440
When the Changding Alley operation
was carried out,

367
00:40:14,440 --> 00:40:15,360
where were you?

368
00:40:19,140 --> 00:40:21,470
I was with Detective Hua Liang
at the time.

369
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:25,220
You can call him yourself to confirm.

370
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,430
There's no need to hide the fact

371
00:40:28,430 --> 00:40:30,230
that you were with him, is there?

372
00:40:34,770 --> 00:40:35,480
General,

373
00:40:36,820 --> 00:40:38,000
I can report this matter

374
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:39,370
to you,

375
00:40:40,880 --> 00:40:42,320
but I can't tell Li Moqun.

376
00:40:45,190 --> 00:40:46,150
Why?

377
00:40:50,610 --> 00:40:52,210
Because Detective Hua Liang

378
00:40:52,840 --> 00:40:56,670
is helping me track down the ledgers
detailing Yu Yingxiang's embezzlement.

379
00:40:56,670 --> 00:40:58,330
Have you forgotten, General?

380
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:02,480
My initial mission when I came to Shanghai
was to investigate corruption.

381
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:04,280
But the situation here is complicated,

382
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:05,320
so I had no choice
but to investigate discreetly

383
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:07,380
and avoid confronting them head-on.

384
00:41:08,110 --> 00:41:09,630
Eventually, I discovered

385
00:41:09,920 --> 00:41:11,310
that the person who killed Yu Yingxiang

386
00:41:11,310 --> 00:41:13,620
was Du Huangqiao, codenamed "Cleaner."

387
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:18,190
He was clearly acting on Li Moqun's orders

388
00:41:18,190 --> 00:41:21,190
to eliminate witnesses,
destroy physical evidence,

389
00:41:23,550 --> 00:41:25,190
and cover up the truth—

390
00:41:25,290 --> 00:41:26,480
all while framing me

391
00:41:26,960 --> 00:41:28,420
with groundless charges.

392
00:41:28,800 --> 00:41:29,930
At the end of the day,

393
00:41:30,480 --> 00:41:34,210
he's simply afraid I'll get in the way
of his money-making schemes.

394
00:41:37,150 --> 00:41:37,880
General.

395
00:41:39,360 --> 00:41:42,760
Where exactly did the 300,000-yuan
special monthly funding

396
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:44,260
allocated to No. 76 end up?

397
00:41:44,880 --> 00:41:46,320
And who's been the one stirring up
so much trouble

398
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:48,520
among Shanghai's business community?

399
00:41:49,370 --> 00:41:51,430
I believe you know the answers by now.

400
00:41:57,880 --> 00:41:59,480
Do you have enough evidence?

401
00:42:01,990 --> 00:42:04,850
I never do anything
unless I'm certain of my ground.

402
00:42:05,550 --> 00:42:07,480
Once I've sorted out the evidence,

403
00:42:07,480 --> 00:42:09,550
I'll report it to the Nanjing government

404
00:42:09,550 --> 00:42:10,840
and the Plum Blossom Agency.

405
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,030
So until then,

406
00:42:12,750 --> 00:42:13,960
I cannot reveal my whereabouts

407
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,760
to anyone involved in the case.

408
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,190
Is that reason

409
00:42:20,550 --> 00:42:22,210
good enough for you, General?

410
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:27,650
I've reported yesterday's situation
to Kagesa,

411
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:31,600
and he agrees with our suspicions
about Su Men.

412
00:42:32,140 --> 00:42:34,000
As long as the Japanese give the go-ahead,

413
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:36,230
we can use every means at our disposal

414
00:42:36,820 --> 00:42:39,020
to pry all of Su Men's secrets out of her.

415
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:45,290
There's one more thing.

416
00:42:45,890 --> 00:42:47,890
Do you know that Cang Guanglian

417
00:42:47,950 --> 00:42:49,390
had a mistress named Shasha?

418
00:42:49,390 --> 00:42:50,060
I do.

419
00:42:51,230 --> 00:42:53,000
That woman took a lot of money from him

420
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:54,670
and has been flaunting it around.

421
00:42:54,670 --> 00:42:55,670
Go take care of it.

422
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:57,510
He may be dead,

423
00:42:58,150 --> 00:42:59,150
but his reputation must remain intact.
